From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rowley <johnrowleyster@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:31:32 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(miniwin): share immediate mode's transform and
 lighting between backends

Move the software backend's per-vertex work for DrawIndexedPrimitive
(transforms, back-face culling, Direct3D lighting with the scene's
prepared lights, vertex fog) and the decoding of the device's render,
light and texture stage states into immediatemode.cpp, so that a GPU
backend can light and cull exactly as the software backend does and only
rasterize differently. The software backend's results are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

